  "description": "An SFTP session is a channel on the same connection as the shell, with its own session id and socket (lang-arch §4.1 sftp.sock; Contract §15: a session). Published at this tag so N channels per connection is expressible from the start (decision 5.21). Not required green: the file surface is a later release's (decision 5.43), and until then a worker may answer error not_supported.",
